{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1262 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "e45dd89b4480e4bb89b764d0b6779a5b55450965c69499b60593f0a8326da074" :edb/db-before-t 1261 :edb/db-after-t 1262 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534574 50 #inst "2026-10-08T01:25:47.713Z" 13194139534574 true] [17592186100806 1020 #edb/ref 17592186296379 13194139534574 true] [17592186100806 1020 #edb/ref 17592186296393 13194139534574 true] [17592186100806 1020 #edb/ref 17592186296401 13194139534574 true] [17592186100806 1020 #edb/ref 17592186296415 13194139534574 true] [17592186100807 1020 #edb/ref 17592186296386 13194139534574 true] [17592186100807 1020 #edb/ref 17592186296389 13194139534574 true] [17592186100807 1020 #edb/ref 17592186296397 13194139534574 true] [17592186100807 1020 #edb/ref 17592186296408 13194139534574 true] [17592186296379 1017 #edb/ref 17592186296380 13194139534574 true] [17592186296379 1089 "q-14313" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296379 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534574 true] [17592186296379 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}$  that satisfies $y(1)=2.$" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296379 1113 #uuid "a5938f28-6b10-54af-bd46-b5bd83651a7a" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296379 1145 "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ {y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={x}^{2} \\\\ \\int {y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{3}}{3} & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+{C}_{1} \\\\ {y}^{3} & ={x}^{3}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere   $C=3{C}_{1}$ is an arbitrary constant.  \n\nWe now apply the condition $y(1)=2$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{2}^{3} & ={1}^{3}+C \\\\ 8-1 & =C \\\\ C & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}={x}^{3}+7.\n$$" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296380 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296381 13194139534574 true] [17592186296380 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296382 13194139534574 true] [17592186296380 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296383 13194139534574 true] [17592186296380 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296384 13194139534574 true] [17592186296380 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296385 13194139534574 true] [17592186296380 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534574 true] [17592186296380 1041 "selection" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296380 1104 #edb/ref 17592186296381 13194139534574 true] [17592186296380 1110 #uuid "1e931c97-953c-5bd7-9dfc-1e428ad98edf" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296381 1034 "{y}^{3}={x}^{3}+7" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296381 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534574 true] [17592186296381 1111 #uuid "d573eb2d-82ab-5413-8bcb-b9b2336a830d" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296382 1034 "{y}^{3}=5{x}^{3}+3" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296382 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534574 true] [17592186296382 1111 #uuid "62ebf476-68aa-5bd7-bff4-c6c6a4b750c3" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296383 1034 "{y}^{3}=2{x}^{3}+2" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296383 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534574 true] [17592186296383 1111 #uuid "98f15021-418c-5d7a-81fc-5a641671a6c9" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296384 1034 "{y}^{3}={x}^{2}+3" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296384 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534574 true] [17592186296384 1111 #uuid "3ef8da88-22a3-5a8a-8a1d-60b6223fcbb8" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296385 1034 "{y}^{3}=3{x}^{2}+5" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296385 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534574 true] [17592186296385 1111 #uuid "f0f49ccd-93ef-5294-bc32-626551ecf864" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296386 1017 #edb/ref 17592186296387 13194139534574 true] [17592186296386 1089 "q-350957" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296386 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534574 true] [17592186296386 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{e}^{-y}=6{x}^{2}{e}^{-y}$ that satisfies $y(1)=0.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296386 1113 #uuid "66d0e457-c6f5-5966-8c94-b8d2ddac2421" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296386 1145 "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{e}^{-y} & =6{x}^{2}{e}^{-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6{x}^{2}{e}^{-y}-{e}^{-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(6{x}^{2}-1){e}^{-y} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =(6{x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (6{x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & =2{x}^{3}-x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{x}^{3}-x+C) \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{x}^{3}-x+C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=0$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\cdot {1}^{3}-1+C) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+C) & =0 \\\\ C & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{x}^{3}-x).\n$$" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296387 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296388 13194139534574 true] [17592186296387 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534574 true] [17592186296387 1041 "field-1" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296387 1104 #edb/ref 17592186296388 13194139534574 true] [17592186296387 1110 #uuid "375c5fbb-2e58-5428-aa32-345b96779d2a" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296388 1034 "\\ln(2x^3-x)" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296388 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534574 true] [17592186296388 1111 #uuid "38cd088b-8c79-5386-a1ca-0b764fdb511c" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296389 1017 #edb/ref 17592186296390 13194139534574 true] [17592186296389 1089 "q-355564" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296389 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534574 true] [17592186296389 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $(-\\frac{1}{xy}+\\frac{2}{y})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4$ that satisfies $y(1)={e}^{2}.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296389 1113 #uuid "0a0c1a6f-49f7-5e1b-8197-0268b6fe21e5" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296389 1145 "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-\\frac{1}{xy}+\\frac{2}{y})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4 \\\\ \\frac{2x-1}{xy}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4 \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{4x}{2x-1} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2+\\frac{2}{2x-1} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =(2+\\frac{2}{2x-1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (2+\\frac{2}{2x-1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =2x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the exponential function to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{2x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-1|+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{2x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-1|+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{2x}\\cdot {e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-1|}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ y & =K(2x-1){e}^{2x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm {e}^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)={e}^{2}$ to find $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & ={e}^{2} \\\\ K(2(1)-1){e}^{2(1)} & ={e}^{2} \\\\ K{e}^{2} & ={e}^{2} \\\\ K & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)=(2x-1){e}^{2x}.\n$$" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296390 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296391 13194139534574 true] [17592186296390 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296392 13194139534574 true] [17592186296390 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534574 true] [17592186296390 1041 "field-1" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296390 1104 #edb/ref 17592186296392 13194139534574 true] [17592186296390 1110 #uuid "96e36a3b-29b9-5717-92d3-0819ec1a5c2c" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296391 1034 "(2x+1)e^{2x}" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296391 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534574 true] [17592186296391 1111 #uuid "e20c6bba-6022-5997-aa9a-58790672ebd6" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296392 1034 "(2x-1)e^{2x}" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296392 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534574 true] [17592186296392 1111 #uuid "36f8ef4a-d466-5e27-9632-1ba0c811f4ad" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296393 1017 #edb/ref 17592186296394 13194139534574 true] [17592186296393 1089 "q-355579" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296393 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534574 true] [17592186296393 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{x}}$  that satisfies $y(1)={e}^{2}.$\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296393 1113 #uuid "d3a0c150-d1a0-56a4-b28e-6e1eb94bcefb" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296393 1145 "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =2\\sqrt{x}+C\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the exponential function to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{2\\sqrt{x}+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{2\\sqrt{x}+C}\\, \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{2\\sqrt{x}}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ y & =K{e}^{2\\sqrt{x}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm {e}^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the condition $y(1)={e}^{2}$ to find $K:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2} & =K{e}^{2\\sqrt{1}} \\\\ {e}^{2} & =K{e}^{2} \\\\ K & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{x}}$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)={e}^{2}$ is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{2\\sqrt{x}}\\,.\n$$" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296394 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296395 13194139534574 true] [17592186296394 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296396 13194139534574 true] [17592186296394 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534574 true] [17592186296394 1041 "field-1" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296394 1104 #edb/ref 17592186296396 13194139534574 true] [17592186296394 1110 #uuid "d4d5d54c-ef9d-5325-a682-474a74c91206" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296395 1034 "e^{\\sqrt{x}}" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296395 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534574 true] [17592186296395 1111 #uuid "3b309eca-74f7-5b49-bd78-db38996b5ee2" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296396 1034 "e^{2\\sqrt{x}}" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296396 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534574 true] [17592186296396 1111 #uuid "2e81344c-5810-55eb-b37a-cd7e5b7b78d5" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296397 1017 #edb/ref 17592186296398 13194139534574 true] [17592186296397 1089 "q-355582" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296397 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534574 true] [17592186296397 1100 "Find the specific solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{-x-y}$ given that  $\\,y(0)=0.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296397 1113 #uuid "fe04fef3-6150-519b-9e35-cabeb0ad595f" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296397 1145 "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x}{e}^{-y} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x} \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & =-{e}^{-x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{-x}+C) \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{-x}+C).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=0$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{0}+C) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(C-1) & =0 \\\\ C-1 & =1 \\\\ C & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{-x-y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=0$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2-{e}^{-x}).\n$$" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296398 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296399 13194139534574 true] [17592186296398 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296400 13194139534574 true] [17592186296398 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534574 true] [17592186296398 1041 "field-1" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296398 1104 #edb/ref 17592186296399 13194139534574 true] [17592186296398 1110 #uuid "800aa3ce-4273-5f23-8ff3-c955acf012d6" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296399 1034 "\\ln(2-e^{-x})" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296399 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534574 true] [17592186296399 1111 #uuid "75d13c89-12e5-5819-b190-541428dbca14" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296400 1034 "\\ln(2+e^{-x})" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296400 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534574 true] [17592186296400 1111 #uuid "32a1d111-a5d3-52c3-9b17-a247a2636772" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296401 1017 #edb/ref 17592186296402 13194139534574 true] [17592186296401 1089 "q-50566" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296401 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534574 true] [17592186296401 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x$  that satisfies  $y(-3)=1.$  Assume that $y>0.$" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296401 1113 #uuid "2bedb039-83dc-5e1b-b856-f023ba4d6c27" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296401 1145 "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x \\\\ \\int y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\text{d}y & =\\int x\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{C}_{1} \\\\ {y}^{2} & ={x}^{2}+2{C}_{1} \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{{x}^{2}+2{C}_{1}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAssuming $y>0,$ the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+C},\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(-3)=1$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+C} \\\\ 1 & =\\sqrt{9+C} \\\\ C & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution of $y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x$ that satisfies the condition $y(-3)=1$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-8}.\n$$" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296402 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296403 13194139534574 true] [17592186296402 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296404 13194139534574 true] [17592186296402 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296405 13194139534574 true] [17592186296402 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296406 13194139534574 true] [17592186296402 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296407 13194139534574 true] [17592186296402 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534574 true] [17592186296402 1041 "selection" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296402 1104 #edb/ref 17592186296407 13194139534574 true] [17592186296402 1110 #uuid "cc0999a9-e763-5a12-a30b-184d1afbb9ea" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296403 1034 "y=\\frac{1}{4}\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}-2}" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296403 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534574 true] [17592186296403 1111 #uuid "5004f8ab-bcfd-5b95-9df0-163643659ee8" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296404 1034 "y=\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}-4}" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296404 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534574 true] [17592186296404 1111 #uuid "6469cc98-0d3e-505a-a4bd-ad22baaed83a" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296405 1034 "-y=\\sqrt{x+4}" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296405 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534574 true] [17592186296405 1111 #uuid "da9e9b0c-b4cd-5345-b2e9-dce18a822acf" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296406 1034 "-y=\\sqrt{2x+7}" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296406 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534574 true] [17592186296406 1111 #uuid "0938ef89-ec65-56dd-9c08-fbac94ee08a8" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296407 1034 "y=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-8}" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296407 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534574 true] [17592186296407 1111 #uuid "ccc6e12d-cbc7-5f30-9434-b017a69c5a0b" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296408 1017 #edb/ref 17592186296409 13194139534574 true] [17592186296408 1089 "q-79371" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296408 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534574 true] [17592186296408 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2x{e}^{x}=3$ that satisfies $y(0)=-3.$" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296408 1113 #uuid "b83618f6-c01a-5048-a3a3-6b622350db67" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296408 1145 "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2x{e}^{x} & =3 \\\\ {e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3+2x{e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{e}^{-x}+2x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3{e}^{-x}+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 3{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-3{e}^{-x}+{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(0)=-3$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =-3 \\\\ -3{e}^{-0}+{0}^{2}+C & =-3 \\\\ C-3 & =-3 \\\\ C & =0\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of ${e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2x{e}^{x}=3$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=-3$ is\n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}-3{e}^{-x}.\n$$" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296409 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296410 13194139534574 true] [17592186296409 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296411 13194139534574 true] [17592186296409 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296412 13194139534574 true] [17592186296409 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296413 13194139534574 true] [17592186296409 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296414 13194139534574 true] [17592186296409 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534574 true] [17592186296409 1041 "selection" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296409 1104 #edb/ref 17592186296411 13194139534574 true] [17592186296409 1110 #uuid "6a28f488-2cc3-5e9b-baa4-b221f207a20a" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296410 1034 "y=4x+{e}^{-3x}-4" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296410 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534574 true] [17592186296410 1111 #uuid "e7a3bc39-a922-5f64-bfd1-2a19006f0aab" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296411 1034 "y={x}^{2}-3{e}^{-x}" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296411 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534574 true] [17592186296411 1111 #uuid "9873e707-2fd2-5249-a343-87db775dbe1e" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296412 1034 "y=x+{e}^{-3x}-4" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296412 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534574 true] [17592186296412 1111 #uuid "96361bee-48b6-5d73-b545-1b1ca709bc20" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296413 1034 "y=-2{e}^{-x}-1" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296413 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534574 true] [17592186296413 1111 #uuid "e083fe15-44ca-5ac8-bc24-f2c898194dce" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296414 1034 "y={x}^{2}-3{e}^{-x}+2" 13194139534574 true] [17592186296414 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534574 true] [1